From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
Subject: econet-eth: keep QDMA NAPI in softirq context

The EN751221 QDMA driver currently enables threaded NAPI on the dummy
NAPI netdev. On TP-Link Archer C5v this shows up as a very regular
latency sawtooth when pinging the router over wired LAN: replies drift
from about 10-11 ms down to 1-2 ms and then jump back up again. With
larger ICMP packets the same pattern can also produce loss.

This pattern is not random link noise; it is consistent with scheduler
or jiffy-aligned NAPI wakeup latency. Keep RX and TX-completion NAPI in
the normal softirq context so packets are processed directly from the
networking poll path instead of waiting for a NAPI kthread to be
scheduled.

--- a/econet_qdma.c
+++ b/econet_qdma.c
@@ -1235,7 +1235,11 @@ struct en75_qdma *en75_qdma_init(struct en75_eth *eth, int id,
 	if (!qdma->napi_dev)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 
-	qdma->napi_dev->threaded = true;
+	/* Threaded NAPI adds scheduler latency on this target; keep the
+	 * latency-sensitive QDMA RX/TX-completion path in softirq context.
+	 */
+	qdma->napi_dev->threaded = false;
+
 	snprintf(qdma->napi_dev->name, sizeof qdma->napi_dev->name, "qdma%d_eth", id);
 
 	err = en75_init(eth->dev, qdma, irqs, num_irqs);
